te":"2016-02-15T12:55:52-08:00","id":830431,"title":"","content":"In the groups I've played, half the time when someone considers Blissful Ignorance, the ST will rule that becoming oddly blurry draws extra attention from people and is a guaranteed veil breach. It's only practically viable in game when you use it to support your normal stealth tactics. Then however, it can be powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/593/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","name":"Taci","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3312_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T13:07:48-08:00","id":830441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taci</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/830299-blissful-ignorance-how-usefu?p=830431#post830431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the groups I've played, half the time when someone considers Blissful Ignorance, the ST will rule that becoming oddly blurry draws extra attention from people and is a guaranteed veil breach. It's only practically viable in game when you use it to support your normal stealth tactics. Then however, it can be powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe you are thinking of Blur of the Milky Eye.<br /> Blissful Ignorance is worded completely differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T13:49:48-08:00","id":830487,"title":"","content":"Blissful Ignorance is pretty damned useful. Do you have to hold still? Yeah. But werewolves are team-players. Have one PC lure some enemies into an out of the way spot so they think they're cornering him... and then his friends with Blissful Ignorance ambush the crap out of them.<br /> <br /> It also has <i>a lot</i> of synergy with other Gifts. A Gnawer with Blissful Ignorance and On Patrol (with appropriate Gift for On Patrol to modify) is kind of nuts in terms of nobody noticing you scanning a full city block.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T23:24:35-08:00","id":830863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <stron